{
  "name": "tools-det (settings > tools page against the seeded governance credential, operator + builder; contract sheet and credential inventory asserted, live test button is a boundary, never clicked)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "tools-empty-reload renders only when governance_list_tools returns an empty list (Tools.svelte:211 `{:else if totalCount === 0}`); the runtime upserts the native tools at boot, so no seed empties the table. The block stubs the command (`stubInvoke governance_list_tools resolve []`) before the first settings-nav-tools click of the book, so loadTools (toolGovernance.ts:30-41) lands on the EmptyState; the first reload click (reload -> loadTools, :190-197) stays empty under the stub, then clearStubs and a second click reload the real list, which the next steps assert as before. Nothing is written.",
    "tools-filter is a bind:value on the toolbar Input (Tools.svelte:224-232): the query feeds rowMatches (:92-101), a query matching only web_search hides the other cards, a no-match query swaps tools-list for the no_results EmptyState (:246-249), and an empty query restores everything. Component state, nothing persisted, no dirty flag.",
    "brave-api-key-delete: remove() (CredentialField.svelte:94-105) calls deleteCredential, which drops the key from the store (toolGovernance.ts:103-115). ToolConfigDrawer receives `tool` as a snapshot prop (Tools.svelte:170 drawerTool, drawer :202-204 braveConfigured), so the row keeps reading configured after the delete; the edit/save path right after re-creates the same key, and the credential inventory asserted later (credential-row-web_search-brave.api_key) is what proves the round trip. Net state after the block: key present, value brave-automation-key-not-real, as before.",
    "brave-api-key-test is played through a stubbed IPC: runTest -> testCredential -> governance_test_credential (CredentialField.svelte:107-121, toolGovernance.ts:118-125) performs a real Brave search with the stored key (commands/tool_governance.rs:490-520), which offline returns ok:false only after the HTTP timeout. The block stubs the command twice, once each: a reject with a raw string lands in the catch of runTest and renders the CredentialErrorNotice under brave-api-key-test-result (its raw detail sits behind a collapsed Disclosure and its friendly text is localized, so that path is asserted by presence, which nothing rendered before the click); then a resolve shaped like CredentialTestResultDto (commands/tool_governance.rs, ok:true latency_ms:12) renders the success line, asserted by the locale-invariant fragment '(12 ms)' of settings.credential.test_valid_ms. The command is cleared afterwards; nothing is written, the seeded credential is untouched, and the delete/re-create round trip that follows runs as before."
  ],
